==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|woosh}}

===Etymology===
Of {{onomatopoeic|en|title=imitative}} origin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ʍʊʃ/|/wʊʃ/|/ʍuːʃ/|/wuːʃ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-whoosh.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
*: {{rhymes|en|ʊʃ|uːʃ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[breathy]] sound like that of an object passing at high speed.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2012|author=John Branch|title=Snow Fall: The Avalanche at Tunnel Creek|newspaper=The New York Times|url=http://www.nytimes.com/projects/2012/snow-fall/?smid=fb-nytimes&WT.z_sma=SP_SNT_20130415#/?part=tunnel-creek
|passage=The snow burst through the trees with no warning but a last-second '''whoosh''' of sound, a two-story wall of white and Chris Rudolph’s piercing cry: “Avalanche! Elyse!”}}
# {{lb|en|MLE|slang}} A [[homicide]] by [[shoot]]ing.
# {{lb|en|MLE|slang}} A [[gun]].

